warning[G006]: incremental unique_key (order_id) isn't unique: the SQL can return several rows per (order_id)
 --> models/marts/inc_order_payments.sql:5:1
  |
5 | join {{ source('ledger', 'payments') }} p on p.order_id = o.order_id
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ one-to-many: rows repeat per row of ledger.payments, so (order_id) repeats
  |
  = note: unique_key = order_id, incremental_strategy: the adapter's default strategy
  = note: two new rows with the same (order_id) make merge fail or pick one at random, and delete+insert keeps both
  = help: set unique_key to the model's key (payment_id), or make the SQL return one row per (order_id), e.g. with a row_number() dedup
  = see: cardinal explain G006

